This supplement reports the artifact-masked re-export `neuralmanifolddynamics_figshare_infant_eeg_20260805_132612` (BAD\_-interval artifact segments masked before epoching, 5,265 epochs; see S1.1). A prior, pre-masking export produced somewhat different numbers for several endpoints; the pre-masking values are noted inline where the change is informative (e.g. S2.5, S2.7) but are not reported in full here.

= S2.1 Cohort-coordinate GEE family (primary result)
Results are stored in `results/figshare_infant_cohort_20260805_132612/03_cohort_coordinate_age/cohort_coordinate_gee_results.csv`. All 12 cohort-coordinate spline models were FDR-supported across 70 visits/22 children. The 3D coordinate results were mobility: $chi^2=11.28$, FDR p=0.011; deviation: $chi^2=54.72$, FDR p=$4.72 times 10^-11$; and entropy-related coordinate: $chi^2=15.09$, FDR p=$2.09 times 10^-3$. The strongest 9D result was $m_o$ ($chi^2=155.37$, FDR p=$2.19 times 10^-32$); the weakest overall was 9D $d_s$ ($chi^2=7.89$, raw/FDR p=0.048). They describe coordinate position in this frozen common chart and are the primary finding of this study (manuscript R2). This asymptotic GEE result should be read together with S2.2 (within/between decomposition) and S2.3 (cluster-permutation check), which qualify how robust each endpoint is.

= S2.2 Within/between-child age decomposition (M3)
Results are stored in `cohort_coordinate_within_between_decomposition.csv`. At every one of the 12 endpoints, the within-child spline term (3 df) is significant: raw p ranges from $7.94 times 10^-73$ (9D $m_o$, the strongest) to 0.0105 (9D $d_s$, the weakest). No endpoint's between-child linear term (1 df) is significant at $alpha=0.05$ after FDR correction; the smallest between-term raw p is 9D $e_m$ at 0.041 (12-endpoint FDR $approx$ 0.21), and most are far from significance (raw p up to 0.98 for 3D entropy-related coordinate). This directly addresses the potential between-child confound: the primary cohort-coordinate result is attributable to within-child movement, not simply to older and younger children differing cross-sectionally.

= S2.3 Child-cluster row-permutation check (M4)
Results are stored in `cohort_coordinate_gee_cluster_permutation.csv` (500 permutations per endpoint, seed 42). Raw permutation p-values, smallest to largest: 9D $m_o$ 0.002, 3D deviation 0.010, 9D $d_n$ 0.016, 9D $e_m$ 0.018, 9D $m_e$/$e_e$ 0.020 each, 9D $d_l$ 0.036, 9D $m_a$ 0.052, 9D $e_s$ 0.056, 3D entropy-related coordinate 0.130, 3D mobility 0.140, 9D $d_s$ 0.222. After BH-FDR correction of these 12 permutation p-values, 6 of 12 endpoints remain supported: 9D $m_o$ (FDR p=0.024); 3D deviation, 9D $m_e$, 9D $d_n$, 9D $e_e$, and 9D $e_m$ (FDR p=0.040 each). Six endpoints do not survive: 9D $d_l$ (FDR p=0.062), 9D $m_a$/$e_s$ (FDR p=0.075 each), 3D entropy-related coordinate and 3D mobility (FDR p=0.152 each), and 9D $d_s$ (FDR p=0.222). This is a materially more conservative picture than the asymptotic GEE (S2.1) and should be treated as the more trustworthy robustness statement given only 22 clusters.

= S2.4 Cohort-coordinate direct-age metadata sensitivity
The spreadsheet-direct cohort-coordinate GEE subset included 40 visits from 22 children. Eleven of twelve endpoints remained FDR-supported; the 3D entropy-related coordinate was the only exception (raw/FDR p=0.070). In 3D, mobility and deviation had FDR p=$6.62 times 10^-4$ and $3.10 times 10^-9$, respectively. Note that 3D mobility is more strongly supported here than in the primary family, despite failing the cluster-permutation check (S2.3), whereas the 3D entropy-related coordinate now fails *both* this sensitivity check and the cluster-permutation check, making it the single least robust endpoint in the full family.

= S2.5 Within-child MNJ and reachability family (robustness check)
All 70 sessions provided a resolved 9D MNJ; 20 children and 68 visits contributed after endpoint-complete within-child filtering. No primary 3D MNJ/reachability endpoint was FDR-supported; the smallest raw p was for the MNJ trace (standardized slope $-0.223$; raw p=0.054; FDR sensitivity p=0.484), whose child-bootstrap interval excluded zero even though the sign-permutation p was just above the nominal threshold. This is not a uniformly clean null: the pre-artifact-masking export had a different smallest raw p (reachability effective dimension, 0.173), while the masked trace result is closer to nominal and should be interpreted with the permutation result and interval together. This is a distinct local-dynamics estimand from the cohort-coordinate GEE (S2.1) and is reported here as a robustness check, not as a primary result.

